LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EZAKI TOMOHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUO TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITOH HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKATA AKIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EZAKI, TOMOHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUO, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHTAKE, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITOH, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKATA, AKIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A bag-like container formed of a synthetic resin, provided with a liquid medicine charging or discharging port member at at least one of the upper and lower ends of the container and having its  bag-like inner surface partitioned liquid-tightly into a plurality of chambers by a blocking seal member; specifically, a multi-chamber medical container excellent in flexibility and transparency and in releasability of a blocking seal member by a pressing operation on a bag member, characterized in that a resin used for the blocking seal member shows a height ratio (h2/h1) of 0.05 to 0.4 between a peak height (h1) at a main melting peak temperature on a melting temperature curve measured by using a differential scanning calorimeter and a height (h2) of the temperature curve at 115  DEG C.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un récipient en forme de sac en résine synthétique comportant un élément à orifice de chargement ou de déchargement de médicament liquide et au moins des extrémités supérieure et inférieure du récipient. La surface interne du récipient en forme de sac est divisée de manière étanche aux liquides en plusieurs chambres par un élément de blocage scellant. L'objet de l'invention se présente notamment comme un récipient médical à chambres multiples qui manifeste une souplesse et une transparence excellentes et une capacité de libération du blocage scellant sous pression, à l'instar d'un sac; il est caractérisé en ce que la résine utilisée dans l'élément de blocage scellant a un rapport des hauteurs (h2/h1) compris entre 0,05 et 0,4, (h1) représentant une hauteur de pointe à une température de fusion de pointe sur une courbe de température de fusion mesurée au moyen d'un calorimètre à balayage différentiel et (h2) représentant une hauteur sur la courbe de température à 115 DEG .</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>